title: 'telegram getUpdates stalls surface as ERROR spam: HTTP timeout after 45.0s ~65 per day'
updated_at: "2026-09-28T02:55:46Z"
---
Observed in daemon.log: 65x ERROR "Telegram poll error for 'default': Failure(\"HTTP timeout in get_with_timeout after 45.0s\")" plus 1x End_of_file, spread across the whole day (roughly every 10-45 min while the daemon was otherwise healthy).

Code: src/telegram_poll.ml:123 calls Telegram.get_updates ~timeout:30; src/telegram_api.ml:52-61 sets request_timeout_s = timeout + 15 = 45s and uses Http_client.get_with_timeout. Telegram's getUpdates long-poll with timeout=30 should respond by ~30s, so a 45s HTTP timeout firing means the request genuinely stalled (connection reuse / pooled cohttp connection gone stale, or network path). Related stall symptoms elsewhere: "failed to fetch PR files: End_of_file" (32x), 180s post_json timeout.

Decisions (already made):
- Root cause may be external (stale pooled connections); fix what we control:
  1. Retry getUpdates immediately (single bounded retry, fresh request) on HTTP timeout before surfacing an error.
  2. Dedup consecutive identical poll errors: log at most one line per 5-minute window per connector, at WARN, with a count; keep ERROR for non-timeout failures (auth, 409, 5xx storms).
  3. Verify the timeout+15 margin is actually applied on the poll path and that timeout param sent to Telegram matches what the poll loop asks for.
- Do not silence real failures: 409 conflict / webhook-active / auth errors must still surface exactly as today.

Acceptance criteria:
1. Simulated consecutive timeouts (mock/fake API returning timeout failure) produce exactly one deduped WARN line per window, not one ERROR per poll.
2. Poll loop survives indefinite timeout streams (no crash, no uncaught exception) and keeps retrying.
3. Single retry on timeout before logging is implemented and unit-tested.
4. make test green; fmt-check clean.

Lane plan: B825 worked serially with B826 in one worktree (both touch telegram files: telegram_api.ml/telegram_poll.ml vs edit path). Parallel lanes: B823 (ec_process/daemon), B824 (memory/ledgers — told to avoid ec_process.ml), B827 (github_api.ml).